/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Nestled in the heart of Himachal Pradesh, Manali is steeped in mythology and natural beauty. Its name comes from "Manu-Alaya," meaning "abode of Manu," the first man in Hindu mythology. Surrounded by snow-capped peaks, lush valleys, rivers, and dense forests, it's often called the "Valley of the Gods.")
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
391 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Must-visit spots include the Hadimba Devi Temple, dedicated to a demoness from the Mahabharata, known for its unique pagoda-style architecture. Nearby, the Vashisht Temple and its hot springs are said to have healing powers. The Manu Temple, dedicated to sage Manu, is the only one of its kind in India. Brighu Lake, where sage Bhrigu meditated, is believed to be sacred.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [1]
>>
